WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:23.064
"I knew she wasn't really a princess," said Jimmy.

2
00:00:23.885 --> 00:00:24.946
The others were silent.

3
00:00:24.966 --> 00:00:27.648
"Can we do anything for you, Mabel?"

4
00:00:28.188 --> 00:00:29.389
Gerald asked kindly.

5
00:00:29.409 --> 00:00:32.272
"If not, we should be going."

6
00:00:33.192 --> 00:00:35.773
"Yes, I want my tea," said Jimmy.

7
00:00:35.793 --> 00:00:39.554
"Tea?" Mabel snapped.

8
00:00:39.574 --> 00:00:42.675
"You'd leave me after getting me into this mess?"

9
00:00:42.695 --> 00:00:44.595
"That's unfair!"

10
00:00:45.075 --> 00:00:45.775
Gerald began.

11
00:00:45.796 --> 00:00:50.377
"We—" "Leave Mabel alone," interrupted Kathleen.

12
00:00:50.397 --> 00:00:53.218
"It must be horrid to be invisible."

13
00:00:53.238 --> 00:00:55.058
"It is.

14
00:00:55.558 --> 00:00:57.979
And it's horrid to have an aunt who doesn't like me.

15
00:00:58.419 --> 00:01:01.840
She wouldn't let me go to the fair today because I disobeyed her."

16
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.422
"You'll have to tell her about the ring," said Kathleen.

17
00:01:06.442 --> 00:01:09.664
"No! Take me with you."

18
00:01:09.684 --> 00:01:14.546
"I suppose you could come home for tea," said Gerald.

19
00:01:14.566 --> 00:01:16.788
"Then we'll decide what to do."

20
00:01:17.788 --> 00:01:20.590
The children agreed that Mabel should leave her aunt a note.

21
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.551
Gerald took out his notebook and pencil.

22
00:01:24.832 --> 00:01:31.356
They watched the pencil move by itself as Mabel wrote: Dear Aunt, You won't see me again for

23
00:01:31.416 --> 00:01:31.796
a while.

24
00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.382
A rich lady in an automobile adopted me.

25
00:01:34.682 --> 00:01:36.043
We are going away on a ship.

26
00:01:36.423 --> 00:01:37.484
Don't try to follow me.

27
00:01:37.844 --> 00:01:42.747
Mabel "But that's all lies," said Jimmy.

28
00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:47.411
"If I said I was invisible, she'd think that was a lie too."

29
00:01:50.173 --> 00:01:52.975
By the time they arrived home, they were very late for tea.

30
00:01:58.538 --> 00:01:59.259
you all right?"

31
00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:00.540
asked Mademoiselle.

32
00:02:01.424 --> 00:02:02.345
"I was worried."

33
00:02:02.365 --> 00:02:05.727
"We're sorry," said Gerald.

34
00:02:05.747 --> 00:02:09.190
"Come in," said Mademoiselle.

35
00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:11.311
"You'll have supper now."

36
00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:26.202
There were only three plates at the table, so Jimmy let Mabel have his.

37
00:02:27.223 --> 00:02:28.404
He shared with Kathleen.

38
00:02:30.204 --> 00:02:34.226
It was strange to see Mabel's food floating in the air and then disappearing.

39
00:02:35.647 --> 00:02:36.688
Everyone was hungry.

40
00:02:41.751 --> 00:02:44.132
The cook grumbled when she had to bring more food.

41
00:02:44.152 --> 00:02:49.475
"It'll be hard to give Mabel breakfast," said Gerald.

42
00:02:49.495 --> 00:02:51.677
"Mademoiselle will be here then."

43
00:02:51.697 --> 00:02:57.160
"We'll have to buy things and feed her in secret," said Kathleen.

44
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:01.562
"Our money won't last long," said Jimmy.

45
00:03:01.582 --> 00:03:04.143
"Mabel, do you have any money?"

46
00:03:04.163 --> 00:03:08.646
"No," said Mabel, "but I've got lots of ideas."

47
00:03:09.687 --> 00:03:12.448
That night Kathleen lent Mabel one of her nightgowns.

48
00:03:13.429 --> 00:03:16.971
As Mabel pulled off her princess clothes, they became visible.

49
00:03:19.173 --> 00:03:21.694
As she put on the nightgown, it disappeared.

50
00:03:22.675 --> 00:03:24.676
She and Kathleen soon fell asleep.

51
00:03:26.412 --> 00:03:31.634
The next morning Kathleen woke to find Eliza, the maid, staring at Mabel's princess clothes.

52
00:03:32.494 --> 00:03:33.835
They were piled on a chair.

53
00:03:33.855 --> 00:03:36.476
"Where on earth did you get those?"

54
00:03:36.996 --> 00:03:37.757
asked Eliza.

55
00:03:37.777 --> 00:03:45.420
"Oh oh someone lent them to me for a play we're doing," said Kathleen.

56
00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.861
She was saved from saying more by the doorbell.

57
00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.582
Eliza hurried away to answer it.

58
00:03:52.542 --> 00:03:56.064
Mabel got up and began to wash her invisible face in the basin.

59
00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:02.421
"I wish you hadn't written such lies to your aunt," said Kathleen.

60
00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:06.642
"What's the use of telling the truth if no one believes you?"

61
00:04:06.662 --> 00:04:09.643
"You should always tell the truth.

62
00:04:10.123 --> 00:04:11.704
Now I'm going to breakfast.

63
00:04:12.164 --> 00:04:15.365
Stay quiet up here, and I'll bring you something to eat."

64
00:04:18.206 --> 00:04:22.387
When Eliza came to make the bed, Mabel untucked the corners of the sheets.

65
00:04:25.648 --> 00:04:26.788
"Drat these sheets!"

66
00:04:27.356 --> 00:04:28.397
Eliza exclaimed.

67
00:04:30.017 --> 00:04:31.478
Then Eliza swept the floor.

68
00:04:31.498 --> 00:04:35.479
"Don't forget to sweep under the rugs!"

69
00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.500
Mabel whispered in her ear.

70
00:04:38.521 --> 00:04:40.882
Eliza turned white and ran from the room.

71
00:04:43.483 --> 00:04:47.845
Meanwhile Kathleen and Gerald had decided they must tell Mabel's aunt the truth.

72
00:04:48.845 --> 00:04:52.767
So after Mabel's breakfast, the children started walking to the castle.

73
00:04:52.787 --> 00:04:57.233
"Mabel, get behind me," said Kathleen.

74
00:04:57.253 --> 00:05:00.217
"Then our two shadows will look like one."

75
00:05:01.578 --> 00:05:06.944
But as they walked through town, a woman noticed a large, black shape on Kathleen's back.

76
00:05:06.964 --> 00:05:08.966
"Hey, missy!"

77
00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:10.288
the woman shouted.

78
00:05:10.308 --> 00:05:12.811
"What have you been leaning against?"

79
00:05:13.912 --> 00:05:15.433
Everyone walked a little faster.
